 6.   The Wilf class in Proposition  5.25 ,
with enumeration  ( 2 j − 1 ) ! 2 (2j-1)!_{2} :  1 , 3 , 15 , 105 , … 1,3,15,105,\ldots  seems to
contain, for any given overlap  m > 2 m>2 , a pattern of any length  K > 2 ​ m K>2m .
Can we find a uniformly described set of representatives, one for each
length? 
 
 
